           "desc": "One of the most important Buddhist sites in Andhra Pradesh, Sankaram is known for its third and fourth century Buddhist structures. The name Sankaram derives from the term Sangharama. Sankaram is famous for the whole lot of stupas, rock-cut caves, brick-built structural edifices, early historic pottery and Satavahana coins that date back to the 1st century CE. The main stupa here was initially carved out of rock and then covered with bricks. Excavations have revealed several antiquities like seals, inscribed tablets, pots, copper coins mostly of seventh century CE.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Andhra_Pradesh/sankaram.jpg",
