@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@
           "title": "Thousand Pillar Temple",
           "name": "Thousand Pillar Temple",
           "desc": "One of the most famous monuments of Andhra Pradesh, the Thousand Pillar Temple, is a twelfth century temple located in Hanamkonda, which was built in 1163 CE by the Kakatiya King Rudra Deva, following the Chalukyan style of temple architecture. The star shaped, triple-shrined temple built on one metre high platform is dedicated to Lord Shiva (Rudreswara), Lord Vishnu (Vasudeva) and Surya . The temple is famous for its richly carved pillars, screens and detailed sculptures, perforated stone screens, richly carved icons, meticulously designed pillars. It has a majestic monolithic Nandi in a highly polished black basalt stone and the 1000-pillared hall architecture.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Andhra_Pradesh/warangal-thousand-pillar-1.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Andhra_Pradesh/warangal-thousand-pillar-1.webp",
