             "desc": "in one of the most artistic crafts prevalent mainly in Buddhist dominated areas like Tawang, West Kameng and Upper Siang Districts. Thangka refers to the flat cloth on which paintings are produced and by extension to the images and paintings themselves. The motif of the painting is mostly on religious subjects along with traditional values.",
