@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@
             "title": "Dances",
             "name": "Dances",
             "desc": "Dance is an important part of the lives of the people of Arunachal Pradesh, performed on various occasions such as rituals, festivals and also for recreation purposes. They vary from highly stylised religious dance dramas of the Buddhists to the martial steps and colourful performances of the Noctes and Wanchos. Both men and women take part although there are some dances such as Igu dance of the Mishmi priests, war dances of the Adis, Noctes and Wanchos, ritualistic dance of the Buddhist tribes, which are performed only by male dancers. The Monpas, besides performing Monastic dances for three days during Torgya festivals, also perform other dances on different occasions. Some of them are- Aji Lhamu dance, yak dance and lion and peacock dances etc. Some of the popular folk dances of the people are Aji Lhamu (Monpa Tribe), Roppi (Nishing Tribe), Hiirii Khaniing (Apatani Tribe), Popir (Adi Tribe), Pasi Kongki (Adi), Chalo (Nocte Tribe), Ponung (Adi Tribe), Rekham Pada(Nishing Tribe), Lion and Peacock dance (Monpa) and so on. Dances are accompanied by songs sung generally in chorus.",
-            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/dance.jpg",
+            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/dance.webp",
             "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
             "materials": ""
           }
@@ -271,7 +271,7 @@
             "title": "Bamboo Craft",
             "name": "Bamboo Craft",
             "desc": "The craftsmen of Arunachal Pradesh make various cane and bamboo articles for domestic requirements. Bamboo and cane are found in abundance in this region due to the heavy rainfall and temperate climate. The tribal population uses these materials almost exclusively for constructing their dwellings, utensils, furniture, and even weapons such as bows and arrows, spears, armor, and implements like dibbles, hunting and fishing traps. Bamboo and cane are also transformed into colorful basket mats, cane belts, attractive smoking pipes, combs, and a variety of household tools and",
-            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/bamboo-craft.jpg",
+            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/bamboo-craft.webp",
             "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
             "materials": ""
           },
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@
             "title": "Arunachal Pradesh - Handicrafts - Carpet",
             "name": "Arunachal Pradesh - Handicrafts - Carpet",
             "desc": "One of the important creative activity in the district of Tawang, is the weaving of carpets. A speciality of the Monpas, the Buddhist community, is that it is done mainly by women. The weaving is done with exotic designs of dragons, geometric and floral patterns.",
-            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/carpet.jpg",
