             "desc": "The practice of making terracottas has been flourishing throughout in Assam since ages and this craftsmanship has transmitted from one to the other. Some of the common figures start from the figures of Gods to mythological characters. The two potter communities namely the Kumhars and the Hiras are living in Assam. The Kumhars use the wheel to produce their pots but the Hiras do not use the wheel. Some of the products are earthen pot and pitchers, plates, incense stick holders and earthen lamps.",
