@@ -400,7 +400,7 @@
             "title": "Assam  Handicrafts -Toys",
             "name": "Assam  Handicrafts -Toys",
             "desc": "Clay toys, pith, wooden and bamboo toys, cloth toys, cloth-and-mud toys are produced in Assam. Human figures like dolls and brides and grooms and a variety of animal forms are the most common forms of toys. The clay toys are in the form of gods, goddesses and other mythological figures. Clays of Pith or Indian cork made in the Goalpara region have been popular for centuries.",
