@@ -412,7 +412,7 @@
           "title": "Kamakhya Temple",
           "name": "Kamakhya Temple",
           "desc": ", situated in Guwahati on the Nilachal hill, is the important temple of the goddess Kali. The temples in the complex are dedicated to different forms of the mother goddess and it is an important pilgrimage. It represents the distinctive Assamese style of architecture. It is said that the female genitalia (yoni) of Lord Shivas Sati fell to the ground while he was carrying her corpse. At that instance the hill turned blue and came to be known as Nilachal (blue mountain). The temple has a beehive-like shikhara with delightful sculptured panels and images of Ganesha and other Hindu gods and goddesses on the outside. The sanctum does not have an image but a spring of water.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Assam/kamakhya_temple.jpg",
