@@ -534,7 +534,7 @@
             "title": "Stonecraft",
             "name": "Stonecraft",
             "desc": "The ancient sculptures of the Mauryan period are witness to Bihar's rich heritage of stonecraft. An outstanding example is the famous Asoka pillar at Sarnath. The most noted stoneware centre of Bihar is Patharkatti in Gaya district. This area is famous for the blue black pot stone from which images and household articles like the pestle or the mortar kharal (medicine grinder) are made. Buddhist sculptures are also made out of this stone. Chandil and Karaikalla in Singhbum district and Dumka in Santhal parganas are famous for the beautifully grained greenish black soapstone.",
