@@ -543,7 +543,7 @@
             "title": "Bihar  Handicrafts -Masks",
             "name": "Bihar  Handicrafts -Masks",
             "desc": "Masks are used for the Chhou dance of Saraikela in Bihar. The Masks are not only very stylish but also equally delicate. The most distinguishing features of the masks are the stylized arch-like eyebrows and elongated half closed eyes. The stylized gestures of the eyebrows, eyes and mouth are painstakingly painted to bring out the distinctive character. These features impart a sense of mystery to the mask. Traditionally only those people who were dancers were permitted to make the masks. Originally they were made of wood, later of bamboo, then pumpkin shells and now papier-mâché. These masks are painted mainly with flat transparent shades and the lines are bold and clear. Avoiding the realistic identification the masks take up a symbolic character.",
