@@ -611,7 +611,7 @@
           "title": "Bihar - Fair and Festivals - Chhath Puja",
           "name": "Bihar - Fair and Festivals - Chhath Puja",
           "desc": "Dedicated to the worship of the Sun God, Chhath is also known as Suryashashti. The word Chhath denotes the number six and thus the festival begins on the sixth day of the Hindu month of Kartik, corresponding to late October and mid November, depending on the year. The devotees take a dip, preferably in the holy river Ganges, observe a fast for the whole day and the offerings are made to the setting sun. Chhath Puja is an elaborate festival noted for its remarkable display of colorful dresses, cuisine, music, singing and extravagant rituals.",
