@@ -661,7 +661,7 @@
           "title": "Chandigarh Museum",
           "name": "Chandigarh Museum",
           "desc": "The Government Museum and Art Gallery, Chandigarh, has a very rich collection of Gandharan sculptures, Pahari and Rajasthani miniature paintings. The six hundred and twenty seven Gandhara sculptures are of various sizes and stylistic denominations. There are some large sized Buddha and Bodhisattva images and also a few depicting Buddhist deities. There are numerous panels showing Buddhist narratives, some of which are of rare variety. The Museum has a good collection of Pahari, Rajasthani miniature paintings and Sikh art displayed in the galleries. Almost all important centres of Pahari Schools are represented in the collection of miniatures. A rich collection of contemporary art including oil paintings, water colour paintings, drawings both black and white and in colour is a highlight of this Museum.",
