@@ -948,7 +948,7 @@
           "title": "Delhi- Monument -Lutyens Delhi",
           "name": "Delhi- Monument -Lutyens Delhi",
           "desc": "From the time the East India Companys first envoy stepped into India during Jahangirs rule in 1616 to the time they left in 1947 the British followed various architectural styles  Gothic, Imperial, Christian, English Renaissance and Victorian being the essentials. In 1911 the King Emperor George V passed an order declaring that the capital of British ruled India would be moved from Calcutta to Delhi New Delhi, was made by the British.",
