           "historical_significance": "1900-1947 Modern",
           "materials": ""
         },
@@ -957,7 +957,7 @@
           "title": "Delhi- Monument- Jantar Mantar",
           "name": "Delhi- Monument- Jantar Mantar",
           "desc": "1700-1750 Medieval The Jantar Mantar built in 1710 by Raja Jai Singh II of Jaipur in Delhi is an observatory consisting of mason-built astronomical instruments to chart the course of astronomical calculations. Jai Singh, who was a very scholarly king with a very keen interest in astronomy and astrology, had other observatories built in Ujjain, Jaipur, Mathura (which no longer survives) and Varanasi Since independence in 1947, New Delhi in particular has grown tremendously as a city and a number of significant architectural projects have been added to its landscape.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Delhi/d_077.jpg",
