           "historical_significance": "1700-1750 Medieval",
           "materials": ""
         },
@@ -966,7 +966,7 @@
           "title": "Delhi- Monument- Birla Mandir",
           "name": "Delhi- Monument- Birla Mandir",
           "desc": "Birla Mandir is the first of the temples built across the country by the industrial family of Birla. Built in 1938, it was inaugurated by Mahatma Gandhi on the condition that people of all castes and especially untouchables would be allowed inside. The temple is designed in the Orissan style, with tall curved towers capped by large amalakas (circular ribbed motif at the summit of a temple tower). The exterior is faced with the white marble and red sandstone and the interior court is overlooked by two-storey verandahs on three sides and has a profusion of sculptures, idols, spires and jalis.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Delhi/d_079.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Delhi/d_079.webp",
           "historical_significance": "1900-1947 Modern",
           "materials": ""
         },
@@ -975,7 +975,7 @@
           "title": "Lotus Temple",
           "name": "Lotus Temple",
           "desc": "The Baha'i House of Worship also known as the Lotus Temple is designed in the shape of a lotus. Its petals are constructed in concrete but are covered with white marble giving an extraordinary lightness to the structure. Nine pools of water around the structure create the illusion of a lotus floating in water. It belongs to the Baha'i Sect and is dedicated to the oneness of all religions.",
