@@ -1033,7 +1033,7 @@
           "title": "Sanskriti Museum",
           "name": "Sanskriti Museum",
           "desc": "Located on the outskirts of Delhi, the Sanskriti Museum is a treasure house of three museums - Sanskriti Museum of Indian Terracotta, museum of textiles and Sanskriti Museum of Everyday Art. Terracotta displays earthen objects made by some of the finest crafts persons, hailing from different parts of India, using their distinctive traditions and techniques. This complex also has crafts persons, where one can see them at work. It exhibits over 150 terracotta items collected from all over the country. The Sanskriti Museum of Everyday Art was set up to preserve the age-old traditions of India. It has functional items of everyday use, like jars, combs, mirrors, toys and kitchen utensils, on its display.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Delhi/Sanskriti_Museum.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Delhi/Sanskriti_Museum.webp",
           "historical_significance": "1980-2000 Contemporary",
           "materials": ""
