             "title": "Pottery and Terracota",
             "name": "Pottery and Terracota",
             "desc": "Goa is rich in pottery which is deep rich red in colour, with a smooth surface, and has a charm and style of its own. A large variety of domestic ware which includes attractive water and flower pots, a wide range of figures and panels are also made including figures of saints and Gods and Godesses and animals, ashtrays and pen holders,etc. These depict an old men or women, mother with a child or two children playing, and a variety of such themes. Borde and Bicholim are two famous centres of earthenware in Goa where both utility cum decorative items are produced by the potters.",
