             "title": "Woodwork",
             "name": "Woodwork",
             "desc": "Goa has an old and rich tradition of wood carving. After the coming of the Portuguese, this craft was turned largely to a magnificent quality in furniture made in western style. However, oriental designs are used in purely floral, animal and human figures. Main places of production are Verem, Bardez and Cuncolim.",
