             "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
             "materials": ""
           },
@@ -1104,7 +1104,7 @@
             "title": "Bamboo Craft",
             "name": "Bamboo Craft",
             "desc": "Bamboo craft is one of the traditional crafts of Goa and practiced in almost all parts of the state. Bambaoo craft in Goa was practiced here by the mahars, a community of Goa. Initially they produced utility items required by farmers and fishermen for drying and storing of food grains and selling fish, etc. The range of items produced during that time and still in use in villages include patlo (baskets), valli (used for washing rice and grains), supli (for cleaning rice), mats of different sizes (used also as shades for windows for protection against rain and sunlight) and dali (one of the most important item for farmers for drying food grains; it can also be used as floor coverings).",
