@@ -1395,7 +1395,7 @@
           "title": "Lakshmi Vilas Palace",
           "name": "Lakshmi Vilas Palace",
           "desc": "is an extravagant building built by Maharaja Sayajirao Gaekwad III in 1890. Right from its imposing façade to its ornate interiors, Laxmi Vilas Palace, Vadodara, is the palace which still serves as the residence of the Gaekwad family. The interiors of the palace radiate opulence and are styled with marble mosaic, fine stone and elegant furnishings. Having a Venetian mosaic floor, Belgian stained glass windows and walls with intricate mosaic decorations, the palace features a grand Durbar Hall which is sometimes the venue of music concerts and other cultural events.. Outside of the Darbar Hall is an Italian courtyard of water fountains. The walls of the Durbar Hall are beautified with brilliant mosaic decorations. There is a commendable collection of old armory,",
