@@ -1416,7 +1416,7 @@
           "title": "Calico Museum collection",
           "name": "Calico Museum collection",
           "desc": "One of the finest textile museums in the world it is housed in a carved wooden haveli. Located in the Sarabhai Foundation, in Shahibagh the Calico Museum of Textiles, was constructed in 1949. Along with the finest collection of not just textiles and clothes the museum boasts of furniture, temple artifacts and crafts of the country. It has a collection of the finest fabrics spun, woven, printed and painted in different parts of India during the last five centuries. One can see the exquisite designs and artwork in kalamkaris, pichhwais, patolas, bandhnis, floor spreads, tent canopies and precious brocades.It has a collection of marble, sandstone and bronze icons and busts split in two thematic sections- gallery for religious textiles and historical textiles. There are colourful embroidered wall hangings depicting legends of Krishna, cloth decorated with tie and dye, glinting mirror work, screen prints, block prints and intricate embroidery. There is an embroidered tent and the robes of Shah Jahan, along with elaborate carpets and plump cushions that once furnished Muslim palace. Special exhibits include Kashmiri shawls, Kullu embroidery, glittering silk brocades from Varanasi, folk art from the Punjab and masks and large wooden temple rathas from Tamil Nadu. The collection also includes some of the best examples of the Patola saris woven in Patan as well as the extravagant Zari work that gilds saris in heavy gold stitching which weigh almost nine kilos.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Gujarat/calico-2.jpg",
