           "title": "Kite Museum",
           "name": "Kite Museum",
           "desc": "Museum situated in Sanskar Kendra the museum was established in 1985 having a fabulous collection of kites from all over the world. There are artistic kites, rare kites that have been crafted from more than 400 pieces of paper. It is the second such museum in the world. Bhanubhai Shah, a conoisseur of kites is the brain behind the concept of the museum and he is responsible for designing and donating kites to the museum. garba dances, mirror work and block prints,the kites are of different styles. The kites are made from different materials as well. The materials include paper, cloth, polythene, and nylon. One of the most lavishly designed and decorated kites are the hexagonal Rokoku - beautiful Japanese kites.",
