           "title": "Gujarat- Museum- Junagarh",
           "name": "Gujarat- Museum- Junagarh",
           "desc": "An ancient fortified city rich in myth and legend, Junagadh has beautiful shrines of Hindus, Jains and Muslims. Deriving its name from the 'old fort', which circles this medieval town, Junagadh was the capital of the Kshattrapa dynasty. The Girnar Hills that landscape Junagadh are a holy refuge to the Jains. The history of Mount Girnar dates back to the empire of Ashoka, who inscribed 14 edicts on a huge boulder en-route to Mt. Girnar peak. There is a huge boulder, housed in a small roadside building, on which are fourteen rock edicts inscribed by Emperor Ashoka.",
