@@ -1501,7 +1501,7 @@
             "title": "Phalgun Dance",
             "name": "Phalgun Dance",
             "desc": "During the month of February March, Phag Dance or Phalgun Dance is performed with joy and vigour. In this dance-men and women group together and involve themselves in a variety of movements, rhythm requiring sound co-ordination. The word Swang stands for disguise or imitation. It is performed in the old tradition on the open stage. It is an all male cultural troupe of twenty to thirty artistes, including the director, producer musicians and actors. The female roles are also played by males. A mutual dialogue between two characters or groups of characters; costumes and music are the main elements of the performance, accompanied by a number of folk instruments like Dholak, Nagara, Tasha, Been, Cymbals etc. Usually performed by villagers, swang is a blend of folklore, music and narration.",
-            "img": "/state-images/Haryana/Ha_016.jpg",
