             "title": "Artefacts & site of Rakhigarhi",
             "name": "Artefacts & site of Rakhigarhi",
             "desc": "Prehistoric 5000 BCE In Haryana, pre Harrapan and Harrapan sites have been found. The major sites from where evidences of civilization are visible are Rakhigarhi, Banawali, Kunal, Agroha, Mittathal and Naurangabad. These sites have traces of paved roads, drainage system, a large rainwater collection and storage system, terracotta brick and statue production, and skilled metal working (in both bronze and precious metals) has been uncovered. Bangles made from terracotta and conch shells, have also been found. Marks of ploughed and cultivated fields, tools for ploughing, stone and",
