           "name": "Haryana-Fairs & Festivals- Gugga Naumi",
           "desc": "The festival of Gugga Naumi in honor of a saint known as Gugga Pir is a festival, celebrated all over Haryana. In the lunar month of Bhadon (August-September) the devotees of Gugga Pir paint his image on the wall in turmeric and worship the snake. They also paint the image of snakes in black color. Milk and butter milk are poured into snake holes.",
