@@ -1735,7 +1735,7 @@
           "title": "Rumaal , V&A Museum Collection",
           "name": "Rumaal , V&A Museum Collection",
           "desc": "The big handkerchiefs called rumals of Chamba are famous and have always been a symbol of love and a good omen. They are presented at festivals and weddings. They are also used for wrapping ceremonious gifts exchanged between the bride and bridegrooms families during marriages. These rumals are embroidered very attractively. The designs show clear influence of miniature paintings. It is done in running stitch without any gaps in between and space filled so that the same figure appears on both sides of the cloth. Rasamandal, hunting, Nayika Bhed, Shiva family and Mahabharata are popular themes embroidered on the rumal.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Himachal_Pradesh/chamba-rumal-bhuri-2.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Himachal_Pradesh/chamba-rumal-bhuri-2.webp",
