@@ -1761,7 +1761,7 @@
             "title": "Ruf Dance",
             "name": "Ruf Dance",
             "desc": "The Ruf Dance is a part of Kashmiri life from time immemorial. The dance has been a part of Kashmiri life from ancient times. This dance is performed to welcome the spring. In the dance, two or four groups are formed consisting of 2 to 3 women. They stand facing each other holding hands of their partner. The women together sway their feet forward and backward. The song sung in the performance is in the form of question and answer form where one group questions and the other respond to it in rhythm.",
-            "img": "/state-images/Jammu_Kashmir/ruf-dance.jpg",
