@@ -1865,7 +1865,7 @@
           "title": "Shankaracharaya Temple",
           "name": "Shankaracharaya Temple",
           "desc": "The temple of Shankaracharya occupies the top of the hill in the southeast of Srinagar where Shankaracharya stayed when he visited Kashmir in the ninth century from Kerala and delivered discourses. Built on a high octagonal plinth and approached by a flight of steps, it has sidewalls that once bore inscriptions and the main surviving shrine consists of a circular cell. A modern ceiling covers the inner sanctum and an inscription in Persian traces its origin to the reign of Emperor Shah Jehan. The original ceiling was dome- shaped and the brick roof is not more than a century old.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Jammu_Kashmir/Shankaracharya.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Jammu_Kashmir/Shankaracharya.webp",
           "historical_significance": "3000-600 BCE",
           "materials": ""
