@@ -1874,7 +1874,7 @@
           "title": "Jammu & Kashmir- Monument- Jami Masjid",
           "name": "Jammu & Kashmir- Monument- Jami Masjid",
           "desc": "Jami Masjid is in the heart of the old city of Srinagar, this is the largest mosque in Kashmir. Originally built by Sultan Sikandar in 1400, and extended by his son, Zain-ul- Abidin, it is a typical example of Indo-Saracenic architecture. It is built around a courtyard with 370 wooden pillars and galleries around it.The principal features of the mosque are the four minars and eight wooden columns as support and a tiered roof capped by a spire.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Jammu_Kashmir/mosque-jami-masjid.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Jammu_Kashmir/mosque-jami-masjid.webp",
