             "desc": "The tradition of making a special type of traditional rag dolls is prevalent in Gwalior.The faces of these dolls are painted beautifully and the eyes are painted in such a manner that they give them a very lively expression. The dolls are dressed in paper costumes in traditional style. The dolls are highly decorated and ornamented. These dolls are popularly known as battubai dolls as they were created by a woman named Battubai.",
