@@ -2440,7 +2440,7 @@
             "title": "Madhya Pradesh- Handicrafts -Maheshwari Sarees",
             "name": "Madhya Pradesh- Handicrafts -Maheshwari Sarees",
             "desc": "The Maheshwari saree in Madhya Pradesh has an unusual origin for it is traced to a generous queen who once ruled over that territory and designed the first saree. Maheshwar, the place itself is a charming one on the banks of the river Narmada. The Maheshwari saree, mostly in cotton is characterised by its simplicity . The body is either plain or has stripes or checks with several variations. A speciality of the Maheshwari saree is its reversible border because of which either side of the saree can be worn. This is locally known as bugdi. The borders have a wide range of mat designs which consists of floral designs, the best known amongst which is the karanphool pattern.",
