             "desc": "The durries of Madhya Pradesh, from Jobat and Tipgaon in the tribal district of Jhabua are well known for their sturdy character and delightful colours. Weaving in Jobat is simple, done on the pitlooms with panja, a woodden apparatus, almost like an extension of the hand, used to pull back firmly and fix the weft yarn in place. These mats are very attractive because of their delightful warm tints.",
