@@ -2524,7 +2524,7 @@
           "title": "Madhya Pradesh- Monument- Indore-Kanch Mandir",
           "name": "Madhya Pradesh- Monument- Indore-Kanch Mandir",
           "desc": "As the name suggests, the full temple is made up of coloured glass. This Jain Temple was built by the Cotton King Sir Hukamchand in the early twentieth century. Inside this Jain temple thousands of mirrors adorn the walls, floor and ceilings, supplemented by brightly patterned ceramic tiles, Chinese lantern-type glass lamps and cut glass chandeliers. The use of glass beads and raised figures produces a pleasing three-dimentional effect. The paintings done in coloured glass depict stories from Jain scriptures.",
