@@ -2542,7 +2542,7 @@
           "title": "Madhya Pradesh- Monument- Mandu",
           "name": "Madhya Pradesh- Monument- Mandu",
           "desc": "Mandu was built by the Paramara ruler Raja Bhoja and was once the capital of Malwa. It was built in the fifteenth century as a summer retreat. Jahaz Mahal is a unique monument in the shape of a ship which connects two lakes Kapur Talao and Munj Talao. Its unique construction shows the taste and the prosperous art and architecture of the past. Jahaz Mahal was built in fifteenth century when the place was under the rule of Ghiyas-ud-Din. Hindola Mahal means a swinging hall. It was built under the rule of Ghiyas-ud-din. The monument is an audience hall which is adorned with wonderful sculptures. The mahal was built with sand stone with beautifully carved columns. To the western front of the mahal there are few other mahals whose identities are not yet unveiled. Champa Baoli is a construction that stands in the midst of the Mahal depicting the past. There is a provision of hot and cold water that are also connected with the underground rooms.",
