@@ -2551,7 +2551,7 @@
           "title": "Gwalior fort",
           "name": "Gwalior fort",
           "desc": "Gwalior is an ancient city which was under the illustrious rule of the Scindias prior to India's independence. Gwalior was once known as Gopadri or Gopachala. It has relics from the period of the Guptas, Huns, Pratiharas, Tomaras, Pathans, Moghuls, Marathas and the British. Among the temples of interest at Gwalior are the Chaturbhuj temple, the Sas Bahu temple and the Teli Ka Mandir. The Chaturbhuj temple dedicated to Vishnu is located on the eastern road to the fort. It is a rock cut monolithic structure and it was built in the year 875 during the rule of the Pratiharas. The Sas Bahu temples are located on the eastern slope of the Gopadri hill. Both of these temples, built in the Nagara style of architecture are dedicated to Padmanabha or Vishnu. Ornately decorated, the doorways, ceilings, and the",
