           "desc": "pillars are covered with intricate sculptural work.The hundred feet tall Teli Ka Mandir dates back to the ninth century and it is the highest building in Gwalior fort. Most of the decorative details in this temple follow the nagara idiom, while the tower is in the dravidian style.Near this temple Also in the fort is the tomb of Tansen, the musician who adorned the court of Akbar. Several Jain sculptures dating back to the fifteenth century adorn the slopes of the hill. Other attractions in the fort include the Gurjari Mahal built by Raja Mansingh during the",
