@@ -2718,7 +2718,7 @@
           "title": "Daulatabad Fort",
           "name": "Daulatabad Fort",
           "desc": "Once known as Devagiri, this place was later renamed as Daulatabad by the then Sultan of Delhi, Mohammed - bin - Tughlak. One of the world's best preserved forts of medieval times the fort has hundreds of secret passages. The fortress was built to be secure with three massive walls to defend it against enemy attacks. The fort has some impressive structures like the Chand Minar, Jami Masjid and Royal Palace which are worth mentioning. The palace also has a few spacious halls, courtyards and pavilions.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Maharashtra/daulatabad-1.jpg",
