@@ -2939,7 +2939,7 @@
             "title": "Textiles",
             "name": "Textiles",
             "desc": "Women weave Endi silk in their spare time using loin-looms. Garos also use frame-looms. Endi silk-weaving is famous for its smooth texture and sturdiness. Cotton with geometrical motifs are also used in clothes worn by the people of this region. Dakmanda, is a kind of blouse worn by the garo women. Daksari is another dress which is wrapped around and looks like the mekhla (dress worn by the Assamese women). Khasi women wear a dress called Jainsem which flows loose up to the ankles. The upper part of the body being clad in a blouse. Over these, they tie both ends of a checkered cotton cloth on one shoulder. The Tapmohkhlieh or head-shawl is worn by knotting both ends behind the neck.",
