@@ -3038,7 +3038,7 @@
           "title": "Mizoram- Fairs and Festivals- Chapchar Kut",
           "name": "Mizoram- Fairs and Festivals- Chapchar Kut",
           "desc": "Chapchar Kut, the spring festival is the most important in Mizoram. People of all ages, men and women, dress themselves in traditional and colourful costumes and wear exotic headgears and jewellery. They assemble and perform various folk dances and also sing traditional songs accompanied by beating of drums, gongs and cymbals. The groups from every region come to the event and display their best performance. The performers dance in joyous celebration of life. Cheraw or the bamboo dance which is popular all over the country is also performed during this festival. The Mizo dances are associated with their respective festival celebrations. More popular dances like the Cheraw are performed almost in every festival of the state.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Mizoram/chapchar-kut.jpg",
