         },
@@ -3067,7 +3067,7 @@
           "title": "State Museum",
           "name": "State Museum",
           "desc": "The Mizoram State Museum exhibits a wide array of costumes, artifacts and historical relics. Glimpses on the traditional clothes, artifacts and historical relics can reveal much of the culture and the heritage of the Mizo people. Some of the weapons that are displayed here have been used in battles fought many years ago. From time immemorial, the Mizo craftsmanship had been recognised by their work in bamboo and cane craft. The best skills of Mizoram craft can be depicted in weaving, pipes, jewellery, musical instruments, bamboo and cane craft. Weaving is an integral part of Mizo life.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Mizoram/state-museum.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Mizoram/state-museum.webp",
