           "materials": ""
         }
@@ -3089,7 +3089,7 @@
             "title": "Nagaland- Performing Arts",
             "name": "Nagaland- Performing Arts",
             "desc": "Tribal dances are performed mainly during festivals, marriages and harvest. War dances, dance during festivals and bamboo dance are some of the commonest. When the ritual is performed, the dancers are usually clothed in colourful costumes and jewellery. Nagaland, with its bountiful resources, makes it excel in the tradition of arts and crafts. With a wide array of workmanship, the delight of the craftsman can be found on the baskets, weaving, wood carving, pottery and metal works, jewellery and bead works. Village gates, house posts and Morungs show true workmanship. Morung are guardhouses, recreational clubs and centers of education used as an important ceremonial domain. Morung may vary in function and size from onr tribe to another. The pillars of Morung are adorned and carved with human figures, tigers, elephants, horn bills, pythons and other designs.",
-            "img": "/state-images/Nagaland/basket1.jpg",
