             "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
             "materials": ""
           }
@@ -3100,7 +3100,7 @@
             "title": "Nagaland- Handicrafts- Basketry",
             "name": "Nagaland- Handicrafts- Basketry",
             "desc": "The cane baskets of the Khonoma village and of the Khiamngan weavers in the Tuensang District are known for their intricate weaves. Fine bamboo and cane strips are also used for making headgear and mats. These baskets are well known for their utility as well as for aesthetic value.",
