@@ -4462,7 +4462,7 @@
           "title": "Tripura Government Museum",
           "name": "Tripura Government Museum",
           "desc": "The Tripura Government Museum is a treasure house of artifacts and manuscripts that are a feature of the rich history of the northeast. A store house of priceless pieces the museum is endowed with four galleries, namely the Archaeological gallery, Tribal Culture gallery Painting gallery and the Indian Sculpture gallery. The galleries showcase a wonderful collection of over 1645 historical artifacts. Scholars and historians can seek numismatic evidence through the numerous gold, silver and copper coins that the archaeological excavations have unraveled. Numerous pottery pieces, sculptures and terracotta, bronze figurines and primordial copper inscriptions have also been unearthed. Magnificent canvas oil paintings, sketches and illustrations, textiles as well as jewellery and ornaments also find pride of place in the museum's sprawling galleries. The museum is also endowed with a library that contains an enviable collection of rare and out print editions on the history, archeology, architecture and anthropology of Tripura.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Tripura/tripura-museum.jpg",
