@@ -4519,7 +4519,7 @@
             "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Embroidery",
             "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Embroidery",
             "desc": "Lucknow's craftswomen are known for their Chikankari. The name chikan seems to have been derived from the Persian word, either Chikan, Chikin or Chikeen. It means a kind of cloth wrought with needlework. A delicate and subtle embroidery, reminiscent of the shadow work of Isphahan in Persia, Chikankari's charm lies in the minuteness, evenness and sheer excellence of craft as well as the use of white embroidery on white cloth. Chief among the stitches are murree, lepchi, keelkangan, bakhia in which forms are outlined on the right side with minute stitches while the threads are concentrated on the wrong side, giving the motifs an opaque shadowy quality. The motifs of chikankari range from floral and vine themes to birds, animals and arabesques.",
