@@ -4528,7 +4528,7 @@
             "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Weaving",
             "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Weaving",
             "desc": "Sari weaving is a cottage industry for millions of people around Varanasi. Most of the silk for the Banarasi saris comes from south India, mainly from Bangalore. Kinkhab is the art of using gold and silver thread on fine silk and cotton to create the rich brocades of Varanasi gold thread on a silver background creates the beautiful shimmering tissues. Breathtakingly beautiful, they are embellished with bird, animal and geometric patterns in the butidar and jaal style.Weavers known as karigars weave saris in workshops known as karkhanas. The design motifs of these brocades are intricate floral and foliage patterns, kalga and bel, and in sari pallaus and dupattas a string of upright leaves called jhalar.",
