@@ -4564,7 +4564,7 @@
             "title": "Pottery",
             "name": "Pottery",
             "desc": "Khurja pottery has evolved a style of its own by raising the pattern with the use of thick slips into a light relief. The shades of the pottery are in warm autumnal colours like orange, brown, and a special light red. Floral designs in sky blue are worked against a white background. A speciality of Khurja is a type of long pitcher decorated in relief by a thick slip. Specialized glazed items like tableware for modern use are produced in Chinhat and Mausalia. A very special kind of earthenware peculiar to Nizamabada and Azamgarh districts of Uttar Pradesh is distinguished by its dark lustrous finish.",
