@@ -4603,7 +4603,7 @@
           "title": "Qaiser Bagh Palace",
           "name": "Qaiser Bagh Palace",
           "desc": "flanked by two mermaid gates (Lakkhi gate) at eastern and western ends. On the right end was Chandiwali Baradari, which it is believed was paved with sliver and the Khas Muqam and Badshah Manzil, were the special residences of the king. During the days of the mutiny Begum Hazrat Mahal held court from here. The buildings at the Qaiser Bagh quadrangle were occupied chiefly by ladies of the Harem. One of his favourite wives Nawab Mashuq Mahal used to live in it.",
-          "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/kaiser-bagh.jpg",
+          "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/kaiser-bagh.webp",
           "historical_significance": "",
