             "desc": "The rural art of Kumaon known as aipana, a local adaptation of alpana, (plaster with fingers) is practiced by the women folk. The other sacred and dainty paintings of this region are the pitha, the seat of Siva worshipped on auspicious days and decorated with geometrical patterns and chowki (seat) of Lakshmi and Saraswati using floral and traditional patterns.",
