@@ -4862,7 +4862,7 @@
             "title": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Wall Painting",
             "name": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Wall Painting",
             "desc": "In the Kumaon region, the usual wall paintings are known as the bar-boond (dash and dot). The pattern is made first by making a number of dots to outline the design and then joining those dots by lines of different colours. Each pattern is known by the number of dots used. For example in the pattern called masti-bar-mat, a composition of ten dots and the colours yellow, red, violet and green are used. The designs are mostly floral and very lively.",
