@@ -4932,7 +4932,7 @@
           "title": "Baijnath Temple",
           "name": "Baijnath Temple",
           "desc": "Kausani has the famous temple complex of Baijnath in the Garur valley of Katyur. A group of ancient temples dating back to the twelfth and thirteenth century line the banks of the river, presenting a beautiful sight. The temples are famous for its carving stone work. The main 10th century temple houses a beautiful idol of Goddess Parvati chiselled in black stone.According to the local tales Shiva and Parvati are believed to have married at the confluence of the Gomati and Garur Ganga. Innumerable tales of Lord Shiva and Parvati make these temples a fascinating",
