             "title": "West Bengal- Handicrafts- Masks",
             "name": "West Bengal- Handicrafts- Masks",
             "desc": "In West Bengal the wooden masks are an important part of the attire of the Gambhira dancers. The Purulia Chhou masks represent gods and goddesses and mark the beginning of spring when episodes from epics are performed. These simple masks are made of papier mache and have a quality of earthiness about them.",
